+# Aegis 4-week LLM Pilot Plan (Claude / Gemini / GPT)
+
## Objective
- Run a focused 4-week comparative pilot across Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini, and OpenAI GPT family to determine best provider per task and define routing rules for Aegis LLM Router.

## Week 0 — Setup (3–4 days)
- Provision API keys and secure storage (Vault) for each vendor.
- Deploy LLM Adapter/Router (llm/adapter) to a sandbox namespace.
- Configure routes (llm/adapter/config.yaml).
- Prepare pilot harness and sample tasks (llm/pilot/tasks.json).

## Week 1 — Baseline automated evaluation (5 days)
- Run automated evaluations using `run_eval.py` across 4 tasks:
  1) Knowledge Q&A (retrieval-augmented)
  2) Summarization (long-document)
  3) Code generation (small functions)
  4) Safety-sensitive instruction (policy brief)
- Metrics collected: accuracy, factuality, hallucination rate, latency, cost.

## Week 2 — Human evaluation & safety tests (5 days)
- Recruit SMEs to do blind A/B/C reviews on a sample set for correctness, helpfulness, and safety.
- Run adversarial prompt injections and PII leakage tests.

## Week 3 — Integration & verification (5 days)
- Test RAG flows and source attribution for Gemini / retrieval stack.
- Test verifier workflow (llm/verifier) with cross-model verification and HIL gating.
- Measure end-to-end latency with RAG + verifier.

## Week 4 — Synthesis & recommendations (3 days)
- Produce per-task scoring using weights:
  - Accuracy/Factuality 30%, Safety 25%, Integration 15%, Latency 10%, Cost 10%, SLA 10%
- Recommend routing rules and ensemble/validator patterns.
- Produce procurement/security recommendations and contracts checklist.

## Deliverables
- CSV/JSON results from `run_eval.py`.
- Human eval summaries.
- Routing config to apply to llm/adapter/config.yaml.
- Evidence entries in MCP for each call.

