+# LLM Vendor Procurement & Security Checklist (Aegis)
+
## Legal & Contractual
- DPA & Data Use: Confirm Data Processing Addendum includes non-training clause (or explicit training permission), retention limits, deletion guarantees.
- Export & Residency: Ensure data residency constraints are covered; request contractual model for not exporting data outside approved regions.
- SLA & Support: Verify enterprise SLA, incident response procedures, escalation contacts.
- Subprocessor List: Request and review subprocessor inventory.

## Security Controls
- Private Endpoints: Prefer VPC/VPN/private endpoint integration (Vertex private service, OpenAI private endpoints, Anthropic private network) rather than public API keys.
- BYOK / Key Controls: Support for BYOK so your KMS/HSM remains in your control.
- IAM & Secrets: Store API keys in Vault. Implement short-lived credentials where vendor supports it.
- Logging & Audit: Ensure request/response logging allowed (for audit) and contractually permitted, or use tokenization/PII redaction if forbidden.
- Encryption: Ensure TLS 1.2+ enforced for in-transit and encryption at rest for vendor logs if stored.
- Redaction & PII: If PII must not be sent, implement local PII redaction/obfuscation or RAG subset selection.
- Penetration & Compliance: Verify vendor certifications (SOC2, ISO27001, FedRAMP if needed). Request recent pen-test reports if available.

## Operational Controls
- Rate Limits & Quotas: Understand per-account throttles and provisioning options.
- Cost Controls: Set quota alarms and per-project budgets; implement adapter cost tagging.
- Model Governance: Version pinning (store model id+sha), review upgrade policy for vendor model changes.
- Monitoring & Drift: Instrument output hallucination/failure rates and create alerts.
- Incident Response: Playbook for data leakage incidents, and ability to revoke keys quickly.

## Governance Requirements for Aegis
- Evidence Recording: Record prompt, response, model id, tokens, and signature into MCP for every critical call.
- HIL Workflow: For high-sensitivity outputs integrate verifier + n8n manual approval before acting.
- Provenance & Non-repudiation: Where outputs are used for decisions, sign and store proofs in Rekor.

